.SH NAME
example_simple3 \- Documentation for selected 3D example programs 
The \fBp4est\fP library comes with various example programs\&.
.PP
They are kept under the subdirectory \fCexample\fP\&. Most have both a 2D and a 3D version\&. When the library is configured \fC--enable-mpi\fP, they can all be run in parallel on any number of MPI ranks, even on small computers\&.
.PP
Before proceeding with the examples on this page, it is highly recommended to get familiar with the programs, starting from 2D examples in \fBDocumentation for selected 2D example programs\fP\&.
.PP
One first helpful program to try out is called \fCp4est_simple\fP (2D version) and \fCp8est_simple\fP (3D version), both under \fCsimple\fP\&. On this page, we showcase some results of 3D example programs further below on this page, and we encourage everyone to play with the command line arguments\&.
.SS "The historic simple example"
The example can be found in \fBsimple/simple3\&.c\fP\&. It is a 3D version of \fBsimple/simple2\&.c\fP The refinement pattern is generated by some hardcoded prescriptions based on a octants's tree number, refinement level and coordinates\&. Please see the documentation under the link for a full list of configurations\&.
.PP
This program creates/refines & coarsens/balances/partitions one of several available geometries specified on the command line\&. As a result, the output VTK files document all the steps of the mesh manipulation process\&.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Example: unit
.PP
Create a connectivity structure for a stand-alone unit cube\&.
.PP
Usage: 
.PP
.RS 4
\fCp8est_simple unit 5\fP 
.RE
.PP
or with MPI: 
.PP
.RS 4
\fCmpirun -np 4 p8est_simple unit 5\fP 
.RE
.PP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
No\&. of trees: 1
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Maximum refinement level: chosen on the command line as 5
.PP

.PP
.PP
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Example: periodic
.PP
Further enriching the upper example, this example program creates a connectivity structure of a unit cube with all-periodic boundary conditions\&.
.PP
Usage: 
.PP
.RS 4
\fCp8est_simple periodic 5\fP 
.RE
.PP
or with MPI: 
.PP
.RS 4
\fCmpirun -np 4 p8est_simple periodic 5\fP 
.RE
.PP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
No\&. of trees: 1
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Maximum refinement level: chosen on the command line as 5
.PP

.PP
.PP
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Example: two wraps
.PP
Further developing the ideas above, this example program creates a connectivity structure of two wrap-up cubes (each of which is a tree)\&. The visually not connected far ends of the two cubes are periodically identical\&.
.PP
Usage: 
.PP
.RS 4
\fCp8est_simple twowraps 5\fP 
.RE
.PP
or with MPI: 
.PP
.RS 4
\fCmpirun -np 7 p8est_simple twowraps 5\fP 
.RE
.PP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
No\&. of trees: 2
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Maximum refinement level: chosen on the command line as 5  
.PP

.PP

